+# Conventional GCC 4.2.1 build wrapper
+
+`build.sh` is the convenience entry point for a normal, non-unified build.
+Run it from an empty out-of-tree build directory.  Keep build trees beneath
+the common `/home/foo/src/builds` directory rather than creating them directly
+in `/home/foo/src`:
+
+```sh
+mkdir -p /home/foo/src/builds/conventional
+cd /home/foo/src/builds/conventional
+../../gcc-4.2.1/build.sh
+```
+
+The default target is `all-gcc`, the default parallelism is one job, and the
+default installed prefix (if installation is requested separately) is
+`/tmp/gcc-4.2.1`.  The wrapper explicitly selects the i686 build, host, and
+target triplets because the 32-bit Etch userspace sees the host's x86-64
+kernel through `uname` when run under bubblewrap.
+
+Targets and conservative overrides can be supplied without editing the
+script:
+
+```sh
+JOBS=2 ../../gcc-4.2.1/build.sh all-gcc
+PREFIX=/tmp/my-gcc ../../gcc-4.2.1/build.sh all-gcc
+LANGUAGES=c ../../gcc-4.2.1/build.sh all-gcc
+../../gcc-4.2.1/build.sh check-gcc
+```
+
+`CONFIGURE_FLAGS` may add configure options on the first invocation.  Delete
+or use a separate build directory when changing configuration; the wrapper
+does not silently reconfigure an existing build.  `MAKE` can name a different
+compatible Make program.  The script requires only the shell and tools used
+by a standard GCC 4.2.1 build.  It has no Python, Perl, or network dependency.
+
+## Running the C testsuite
+
+After building the Etch-native Tcl, Expect, and DejaGnu tools in
+`/home/foo/src/test_deps`, run this from the configured build directory:
+
+```sh
+../../gcc-4.2.1/check.sh
+```
+
+The default target is `check-gcc`.  The wrapper prepends
+`/tmp/test_tools/bin`, selects the C locale, and uses `make -k` so one test
+failure does not suppress later groups.  `TEST_TOOLS` may select another
+test-tool prefix, and explicit Make targets may follow the script name.
