+# GCC 4.2.1 Etch testsuite report — 2026-08-01
+
+## Result
+
+The complete C compiler testsuite ran successfully enough to establish the
+vanilla conventional-build baseline:
+
+```text
+# of expected passes        42139
+# of expected failures        116
+# of unresolved testcases       1
+# of untested testcases         28
+# of unsupported tests         293
+```
+
+There are no unexpected `FAIL`, `XPASS`, or `ERROR` results.  The one
+`UNRESOLVED` line follows an expected compiler failure and is explained below.
+
+## Test harness
+
+The already-downloaded source payload was copied from the Jammy i386 chroot to
+Etch's `/home/foo/src/test_deps`.  It contains Tcl 8.6.12, Expect 5.45.4, and
+DejaGnu 1.6.2.  `build-test-tools-etch.sh` builds all three inside Etch and
+installs native 32-bit i386 programs under `/tmp/test_tools`.
+
+Etch does not provide `xz`, so the copied Ubuntu `.debian.tar.xz` packaging
+patches could not be unpacked there.  They are optional packaging deltas, not
+test-harness build dependencies.  The upstream `.orig.tar.gz` sources built
+and passed their installed version checks without fetching or installing any
+additional software.  Explicit `i686-pc-linux-gnu` build/host triplets avoid
+misconfiguration from the x86-64 host kernel identity visible through bwrap.
+
+The DejaGnu install printed a warning when `install-info` could not back up an
+Info directory to `/var/backups/infodir.bak`.  The warning only concerns Info
+documentation; `runtest`, Expect, Tcl, and all runtime libraries were installed
+and subsequently ran the GCC suite.
+
+## Invocation and artifacts
+
+The tested compiler is the isolated conventional build at:
+
+```text
+/home/foo/src/unified_cc1_artifacts/reference-build
+```
+
+The equivalent checked-in invocation is to enter that configured build
+directory and run `../gcc-4.2.1/check.sh`.  The actual run used:
+
+```text
+PATH=/tmp/test_tools/bin:$PATH
+LANG=C LC_ALL=C
+make -k check-gcc
+```
+
+Raw outputs remain outside the repository:
+
+```text
+/home/foo/src/unified_cc1_artifacts/check-gcc-2026-08-01.log
+/home/foo/src/unified_cc1_artifacts/reference-build/gcc/testsuite/gcc/gcc.sum
+/home/foo/src/unified_cc1_artifacts/reference-build/gcc/testsuite/gcc/gcc.log
+/home/foo/src/test_deps/build-test-tools-etch.log
+```
+
+## The one unresolved result
+
+The only unresolved line is:
+
+```text
+gcc.c-torture/execute/mayalias-2.c execution, -O3 -g
+```
+
+At that setting, GCC reports an internal compiler error in
+`splice_child_die` at `dwarf2out.c:5565`.  The testsuite marks that compilation
+`XFAIL`, so it is one of the 116 expected failures.  The old torture execution
+driver then records the corresponding execution as `UNRESOLVED` because no
+executable exists.  The same test passes compilation and execution at `-O0`,
+`-O1`, `-O2`, `-O3 -fomit-frame-pointer`, and `-Os`.
+
+This is therefore a known/expected GCC 4.2.1 debug-information failure plus a
+testsuite accounting artifact, not a missing dependency, target mismatch, or
+change made on `unified_cc1`.  It should remain in the baseline comparison for
+future unified builds: a unified compiler is expected to reproduce or improve
+this result, and must not introduce additional unexpected outcomes.
