+# Full standalone-unified cc1 check — 2026-08-02
+
+## Reason for rerun
+
+The previous fully unified check was interrupted when
+`gcc.dg/20050111-1.c` first exposed an internal compiler error.  Although the
+harness uses `make -k check-gcc`, that option can only continue while the
+process is left running.  This clean rebuild and check were deliberately
+allowed to reach the final DejaGnu summary so later failures would not remain
+hidden.
+
+## Clean rebuild
+
+All artifacts were rebuilt beneath the single directory:
+
+```text
+/home/foo/src/builds/unified-full-check
+```
+
+`build-cc1-unified.sh` completed from the empty tree.  Its one GCC invocation
+for `gcc/cc1_unified.c` took 30 seconds and the resulting compiler passed the
+build script's smoke test.  The unified executable used by this run has
+SHA-256:
+
+```text
+23fc4fe93b5bf308ca00c85b040da5bc98ba702be847cd4f5fcdd3186f2e6529
+```
+
+The conventional C-only driver and runtime harness was then rebuilt in the
+same out-of-tree directory.
+
+Before the full suite, `gcc.dg/20050111-1.c` was compiled directly with
+`-O2 -march=i686`.  Conventional cc1 succeeded.  The clean unified cc1
+reproduced the internal consistency failure, proving that the earlier result
+was neither the known `mayalias-2.c` baseline failure nor stale build state.
+
+## Complete invocation and result
+
+The checked-in `check-cc1-unified.sh` wrapper ran `make -k check-gcc` through
+the final summary.  It restored conventional `gcc/cc1` after comparison
+failed, and left no saved replacement file behind.
+
+```text
+# of expected passes        41143
+# of unexpected failures      507
+# of expected failures         116
+# of unresolved testcases        1
+# of untested testcases         504
+# of unsupported tests          293
+```
+
+The 116 XFAIL results and sole `mayalias-2.c` UNRESOLVED result are unchanged
+from the conventional baseline.  The new results fall into three categories:
+
+1. `gcc.dg/20050111-1.c` contributes two FAIL lines: its internal compiler
+   error and the consequential excess-errors result.
+2. All 36 `gcc.dg/pch` header cases fail in `pch_init` at `c-pch.c:135` for
+   seven option variants.  Each invocation contributes an ICE and an
+   excess-errors line, totalling 504 FAIL lines.  Their missing follow-on PCH
+   checks account for the rise from 28 baseline UNTESTED results to 504.
+3. `gcc.target/i386/lea.c` compiles without diagnostic error but contributes
+   one `scan-assembler leal` failure.
+
+This complete run disproves the earlier working assumption that
+`20050111-1.c` might be the only outstanding regression.  The PCH failures
+are highly repetitive and should be treated as one common `pch_init` defect,
+not as 504 independent compiler bugs.
+
+## External evidence
+
+Generated logs and result files remain outside Git:
+
+```text
+/home/foo/src/builds/unified-full-check/build-cc1-unified-2026-08-02.log
+/home/foo/src/builds/unified-full-check/build-conventional-harness-2026-08-02.log
+/home/foo/src/builds/unified-full-check/check-cc1-unified-full-2026-08-02.log
+/home/foo/src/builds/unified-full-check/gcc/testsuite/gcc/gcc.log
+/home/foo/src/builds/unified-full-check/gcc/testsuite/gcc/gcc.sum
+/home/foo/src/builds/unified-full-check/repro-20050111/
+```
+
+Their relevant SHA-256 values are:
+
+```text
+3a50f1333be03f6c10bbfba0d04edceadb611874520fee91e35bbcfc639a025d  gcc.sum
+cf9738782a8d737a7c5f6a65addce8f039800416a03e883f329e4916bf07dd97  gcc.log
+f4b0f9f994cd0714b44b5e5c201c969b4566c83f5ad74ac05745342cca054f06  check log
+```
+
+## Next diagnostic order
+
+1. Diagnose the common `c-pch.c:pch_init` unity failure with one targeted PCH
+   case, then run the targeted PCH group.
+2. Diagnose `gcc.dg/20050111-1.c` independently in the RTL life/peephole path.
+3. Compare unified and conventional assembly for `gcc.target/i386/lea.c`.
+4. After all three categories pass targeted checks, rerun the full C suite.
+
